; Au. proton-79. period 6, transition metal. valence: 1 or 3.
; most malleable and ductile metal. does not tarnish or corrode.
; excellent conductor. used in electronics for reliable connections.
; catalysis: gold nanoparticles catalyse reactions at room temperature.
; Au³⁺ in medicine: gold compounds used in rheumatoid arthritis treatment.
; formed only in neutron star mergers (r-process nucleosynthesis) — not in stars.
; relativistic effects make Au yellow (not silver-white like most metals).

(kosha gold
  (sthita element domain-chemistry)
  (swarupa proton-seventy-nine transition-metal corrosion-resistant malleable conductor)
  (yukta valence-one valence-three)
  (phala neutron-star)
  (siddha r-process))
